in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl
in @optics/lens
in @mirror/spectral/observation
in @io

# @optics/lens/features — second species under @optics/lens.
#
# The SECOND substrate-decl species discharging Foster's (get, put)
# pair; sibling to @optics/lens/diff (`7e5c298`). Where diff fixes the
# linear carrier to unified-diff bytes and the semantic carrier to a
# peer's @bauchladen.tray (closing the operator-visible arm of Blocker
# 2), THIS species fixes the semantic carrier to `graph_observation` —
# the 16-dim structured record declared at `@mirror/spectral/
# observation` — and closes the fate-consumable arm: mission_text
# bytes lens-project to the observation Fate's 5-layer D²NN reads at
# input-layer altitude (recognition #58).
#
# === Substrate-decl authority ===
#
# Canonical spec:  Mara iter-27, `ec6dbaa` —
#   `docs/specs/optics-lens-features-species.md` (species shape,
#   composition, v0 stub semantics, gauge-theoretic recognition
#   §6: @nl IS @magic at text altitude).
# Adjudication:    Seam Phase D, `d9b7c35` —
#   `docs/audits/2026-07-11-seam-phase-d-optics-lens-features-
#   adjudication.md`. Seam's three verdicts SUPERSEDE parts of iter-27;
#   THIS shard honors them verbatim.
# Boundary scout:  Taut iter-14, `b5619ab` — Q2 graph_observation
#   reuse (58th+ substrate-already-had-the-word instance) + Q3
#   adapter-cascade pattern evidence.
# Family root:     `b0427fd` Mara iter-25 (shards/optics/lens.mirror).
# Sibling species: `7e5c298` Mara iter-26 (shards/optics/lens/
#   diff.mirror; the shape pattern this species mirrors).
#
# === Seam-honoring (verbatim from `d9b7c35`) ===
#
# **Adj 1 — v0 stub:** REJECT blake3-as-Features. Blake3 IS @magic at
# `@mirror/store` altitude (sealing content-identity via the
# Merkle-DAG), NOT at `@mirror/spectral/observation` altitude
# (structured semantic observation). Casting `blake3(text)` as a
# `graph_observation` is a type-lie: the resulting 16 f64s witness
# neither `query_intensity` nor `partition_risk` nor any of the 14
# other NAMED quadrants. Substrate-honest v0 IS `Features::default()`
# — all zeros ≡ Fate::untrained baseline ≡ "no observation yet". The
# Rust discharge (`bootstrap/src/optics/lens/features.rs`) returns
# `Features::default()` at v0.
#
# **Adj 2 — carrier:** REUSE `graph_observation` from
# `@mirror/spectral/observation`. The 16-dim structured record with
# four NAMED semantic quadrants (settlement / crystal / query /
# spectral, four features each) IS the substrate-altitude form of
# Fate's `Features = [f64; 16]` per recognition #58 v1 closure
# (observation.mirror line 30). Declaring `type feature_vector = ref`
# in parallel would be the 58th+ instance of substrate-already-had-
# the-word drift; THIS species refuses.
#
# **Adj 3 — @nl-imports-@magic composition:** ADAPTER cascade,
# separate landing. `@nl IS @magic at text altitude` (iter-27 spec §6)
# DOES NOT justify decorating `shards/nl.mirror` with `in @magic` —
# the same decorative-inheritance pattern Seam refused at tick 15
# (@magic/distinction) and tick 23+ (@magic/frame). The correct
# composition IS a follow-on adapter at `shards/magic/nl.mirror`,
# matching @magic/{distinction,frame} shape verbatim. THAT adapter is
# NOT this shard's burden. Consequently THIS shard does NOT declare
# `in @magic/contract` — the extractor pipeline composes THROUGH the
# adapter cascade at v1 encoder tick, not through decorative parents.
#
# === Blocker 2 fate-consumable arm ===
#
# Alex directive (parent shard iter-25): @fate ↔ linear format gap.
# Sibling diff closes the operator-visible arm (bauchladen ↔ diff_bytes
# at @io altitude). THIS species closes the fate-consumable arm
# (mission_text ↔ graph_observation at @mirror/spectral/observation
# altitude). Together they form the closed autopoietic loop:
#
#   Forward:
#     mission_text
#       |> @optics/lens/features.get  # text -> graph_observation
#       |> @fate.select               # 5-layer D²NN reads 16 quadrants (#58)
#       |> Decision.model             # bundle-tower binding -> prism-op
#       |> @optics/lens/diff.get      # bauchladen -> diff_bytes
#       |> @io.write(stdout)          # operator reads
#
#   Feedback:
#     (edited_observation, old_mission_text)
#       |> @optics/lens/features.put  # observation + text -> text'
#       |> @fate.select               # next candidate re-reads observation
#
# The `put` direction is the autopoietic-closure hop at text altitude:
# operator edits a quadrant on the eigenboard (e.g. raises
# `query_intensity`), `put` re-projects that as revised mission-text,
# `get` re-extracts, fixed-point iteration converges under the
# specified edit-trace regime.
#
# === Sibling relationship ===
#
# Same parent, disjoint carriers, dual altitudes.
#
#   Aspect              | @optics/lens/diff       | @optics/lens/features
#   --------------------|-------------------------|-----------------------
#   Semantic carrier    | bauchladen_state (peer) | graph_observation (Fate)
#   Linear carrier      | diff_bytes              | mission_text (ref)
#   Consumer            | operator terminal (@io) | fate.select (matter-side)
#   Autopoietic closure | diff-edit convergence   | dimension-edit convergence
#
# Both witness Foster laws; both discharge autopoietic closure via a
# species-specific bilateral parallel to but distinct from the parent's
# three abstract bilaterals. The sibling-pair is the second point on
# the Hutchinson attractor the parent flags at §Gaps; the actual
# `split`-composition attractor witness is a follow-on tick.
#
# === Ancestry rationale ===
#
# - `in @prism`                       five-op algebra ancestor.
# - `in @glass`                       verdict carrier for Foster
#                                     bilaterals + autopoietic closure.
# - `in @meta`                        substrate-decl altitude.
# - `in @nl`                          `# <text>` -> nl_literal for
#                                     docblock terms (SAME role as
#                                     parent family-root; NOT the
#                                     extractor-pipeline surface —
#                                     that composes through the
#                                     adapter cascade per Seam Adj 3).
# - `in @optics/lens`                 PARENT family-root (`b0427fd`).
# - `in @mirror/spectral/observation` source of `graph_observation`
#                                     per Seam Adj 2.
# - `in @io`                          linearization crossing at INPUT
#                                     side; mission_text bytes cross
#                                     the @io fault plane when Fate
#                                     reads them (@io is bidirectional).
#
# Notably NOT declared per Seam Adj 3:
# - NOT `in @magic/contract` — the surface↔mechanism bind lives at the
#   @magic/nl adapter cascade (forward-promised), not on this species.
# - NOT decorating `shards/nl.mirror` with `in @magic` — the
#   decorative-inheritance route Seam refused at ticks 15 + 23+.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optics-lens-features-species.md (Mara
#               iter-27, `ec6dbaa`).
# Parent shard: shards/optics/lens.mirror (Mara iter-25, `b0427fd`).
# Sibling shard: shards/optics/lens/diff.mirror (Mara iter-26,
#               `7e5c298`).
# Carrier shard: shards/mirror/spectral/observation.mirror
#               (recognition #58 v1 closure).
# Adjudication:  docs/audits/2026-07-11-seam-phase-d-optics-lens-
#               features-adjudication.md (Seam `d9b7c35`).
# Boundary scout: docs/scouts/2026-07-11-taut-optics-lens-features-
#               family-scout.md (Taut `b5619ab`).
# Substrate decisions:
#   [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#   [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#   [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]] (#57),
#   [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]],
#   [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58; the D²NN input-
#      layer observation this species supplies),
#   [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (Seam Adj 2 58th+
#      instance),
#   [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (Seam Adj 1: v0 =
#      Features::default(), NOT type-lie via blake3).
# Related shards: optics/lens.mirror (parent),
#                 optics/lens/diff.mirror (sibling),
#                 mirror/spectral/observation.mirror (carrier),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (blake3 lives HERE at content-
#                   address altitude per Seam Adj 1 — NOT here),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror + magic/frame.mirror
#                   (adapter-cascade precedent for @magic/nl),
#                 nl.mirror (surface source; NOT decorated with
#                   in @magic per Seam Adj 3).
# Path-namespace: shards/optics/lens/features.mirror declares
# `@optics/lens/features` and only that.

prism @optics/lens/features {
  focus features
  project features
  split features
  shift features
  settle features
}

# === Type carriers (Seam Adj 2 — reuse graph_observation) ===
#
# Parent `@optics/lens` (`b0427fd`) declares:
#   type lens_get     = ref
#   type lens_put     = ref
#   type lens_witness = ref
#
# Sibling `@optics/lens/diff` fixes the linear-carrier as
# `type diff_bytes = ref`.
#
# THIS species reuses `graph_observation` from
# `@mirror/spectral/observation` (imported above) — the 16-dim
# structured record with four NAMED semantic quadrants (settlement /
# crystal / query / spectral). Per Seam Adj 2, declaring
# `type feature_vector = ref` in parallel would be substrate-already-
# had-the-word drift; refused. The mission_text linear-carrier is
# inherited as `ref` from the parent's lens_get / lens_put shape.
#
# Equality on Foster-law RHS: mission_text = byte-equality on
# `@mirror/store` OIDs per Reed math §3.2; observation = field-wise
# unit_interval equality inherited from `@mirror/spectral/observation`.

# === Actions (specialize parent get / put) ===
#
# Parent declares `get(semantic: ref) -> ref` and `put(linear: ref,
# old_semantic: ref) -> ref` with `\ {}` stubs. This species
# specializes the SEMANTIC carrier to `graph_observation` and keeps
# the LINEAR mission_text as `ref`. Bodies `\ {}` stubs per two-tick
# discipline; Rust discharge (`bootstrap/src/optics/lens/features.rs`)
# is one further tick.
#
# `get(mission_text) -> graph_observation` — extract the 16-dim
# structured observation from mission-text bytes. `focus` in the
# five-op mapping: converging pass, text -> single 16-dim record for
# Fate's D²NN input layer (recognition #58).
#
# Per Seam Adj 1, the v0 Rust discharge returns `Features::default()`
# (all zeros ≡ Fate::untrained baseline ≡ "no observation yet"). THIS
# is the substrate-honest v0 at `@mirror/spectral/observation`
# altitude. Blake3 lives at `@mirror/store` altitude — a different
# @magic instance at a different altitude; type-lie here. The v0 -> v1
# lift populates the 16 quadrants from named text-signals (Seam §4
# Tick D: one quadrant per landing tick — `query_intensity` from
# token count, `partition_risk` from spec_oid collision test, etc.)
# once the @magic/nl adapter cascade lands.
#
# `put(observed, mission_text) -> mission_text'` — integrate operator-
# adjusted observation back into revised mission-text bytes. `settle`
# in the five-op mapping: reflecting-back-and-stabilizing pass,
# observation + base -> new text = autopoietic-closure fixed-point at
# text altitude. THIS closes the fate-consumable arm of Blocker 2.
# Under v0, `put` returns identity(mission_text) — `Features::default()`
# has no non-trivial inverse; operator observation-edits are DROPPED
# at v0. V1 encoder discharges `put` operationally.

get(mission_text: ref) -> graph_observation { \ {} }
put(observed: graph_observation, mission_text: ref) -> ref { \ {} }

# === Bilateral properties (Foster laws specialized) ===
#
# Parent declares three abstract Foster bilaterals returning
# `verdict`; this species specializes the OBSERVATION-arg type to
# `graph_observation` (mission_text stays `ref`). Bodies `\ {}` stubs
# per two-tick discipline. `lens_witness` inherited unchanged.
#
# `put_get_features` (PutGet, "acceptance"): `get(put(v, s)) == v` for
# all graph_observation v and mission_text s — putting an observation
# and re-getting recovers it. Lens forward = right-inverse of backward.
#
# `get_put_features` (GetPut, "stability"): `put(get(s), s) == s` —
# round-trip on an unedited observation is text-identity; lens does
# not spuriously rewrite the operator's mission when no observation
# edit was made.
#
# `put_put_features` (PutPut, "very well-behaved"): `put(v', put(v,
# s)) == put(v', s)` — successive observation-edits collapse to the
# last edit; autopoietic-closure semantics insensitive to intermediate
# history.

put_get_features(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: graph_observation) -> verdict { \ {} }
get_put_features(l: lens_witness, s: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }
put_put_features(l: lens_witness, s: ref, v: graph_observation, v_prime: graph_observation) -> verdict { \ {} }

# === Autopoietic closure (parallel to sibling diff) ===
#
# Foster laws are NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT for autopoietic closure
# at species altitude. This bilateral witnesses that the ITERATED loop
# CONVERGES — that under a specified edit-trace regime, the sequence
# (get, put, get, put, ...) at features altitude reaches an operator-
# satisfaction fixed-point in finite iterations.
#
# Where sibling `@optics/lens/diff.autopoietic_closure` (`7e5c298`)
# witnesses substrate learning through diff-edits, THIS bilateral
# witnesses substrate learning through dimension-edits (operator
# moves a quadrant slider on the eigenboard; observation feeds Fate;
# Fate's Decision reshapes the next mission_text). Same shape, dual
# altitudes: diff at @io altitude, features at text↔observation
# altitude. Per Reed math §4.1 (Banach contraction), each `put`
# supplies a fresh basepoint for `Φ = extract ∘ integrate`.
#
# The `edit_trace` argument is a `ref` handle into `@mirror/store`
# carrying the sequence of operator-edits at observation altitude
# across a bounded epoch; returns `pass` when edit-magnitudes contract
# toward zero within tolerance, `partial(confidence)` when contraction
# is soft/slow, `failure(reason)` when the trace diverges or oscillates.
#
# Body `\ {}` stub per two-tick discipline; Seam Phase E audit gates
# the discharge once @magic/nl adapter + v1 encoder land.

features_autopoietic_closure(l: lens_witness, edit_trace: ref) -> verdict { \ {} }

# === Exports ===

out @optics/lens/features
out get
out put
out put_get_features
out get_put_features
out put_put_features
out features_autopoietic_closure

